NAME
       mkdir - make directories

SYNOPSIS
       mkdir [-p] [-m MODE] [-v] [-Z] DIRECTORY...

DESCRIPTION
       mkdir creates each DIRECTORY. The parent directory must exist, unless
       you add -p. New directories get mode 777 minus the umask (755 with
       the usual umask 022), the creator as owner, and the SELinux context
       that the parent directory passes on.

OPTIONS
       -p, --parents
              Create missing parent directories too, and do not complain when
              the directory exists already.

       -m, --mode MODE
              Set the permissions (octal or symbolic) instead of using the
              umask, such as -m 2770.

       -v, --verbose
              Print each directory created.

       -Z     Give the directory the default SELinux context of its path.

EXAMPLES
       Make a nested path in one step:

           mkdir -p /srv/projects/2026/reports

       A shared group directory where new files belong to the group:

           mkdir -m 2770 /srv/team
           chgrp devs /srv/team

       Several directories at once, with brace expansion:

           mkdir -p ~/lab/{in,out,tmp}

SEE ALSO
       rmdir(1), chmod(1), umask(1), install(1)
